></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">(</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.56em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:3.62em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-1.56em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.06em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.71em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.06em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.92em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.06em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.12em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.06em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.56em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[75]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{nu} & \\text{\\#solutions (free subleading)} & \\text{actual subleading (s1, s2, s3)} & \\text{formula at nu} & \\text{permutations of nu reproducing it}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,2,1,0\\right\\} & 2 & \\begin{pmatrix}-5.905929 & -29.71663 & -13.90593\\end{pmatrix} & \\left\\{-5.905929,-29.71663,-13.90593\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 2 & \\begin{pmatrix}-5.906596 & -29.71796 & -13.90660\\end{pmatrix} & \\left\\{-5.906596,-29.71796,-13.90660\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}2 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "3195b02a-0282-4a2e-8ded-836bf0241fb0"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: the degenerate partners of `{2,1,1,0}` (cell 11, after the fix)\n\n| ε | partners | max \\|M'(0)·w/ε\\| / \\|w/ε\\| | singular values of the partner directions |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10⁻³ | 14 | 0.061 | 3.309, 1.747, 2.2×10⁻⁴, 1.7×10⁻⁴, … |\n| 10⁻⁴ | 14 | 0.0061 | 3.309, 1.746, 2.2×10⁻⁵, 1.0×10⁻⁵, … |\n\nThe 14 partners are exactly the rest of the 15-dimensional multiplet: the 11 other permutations of `{2,1,1,0}` and 3 states at `{1,1,1,1}`. The residual falls like `ε`, and two singular values stay fixed while the rest fall like `ε`. So the limits `w(A,A')/ε` span a 2-dimensional subspace of `ker M'^{AA}(0)`, which is 2-dimensional. **The zero-twist kernel of `{2,1,1,0}` is spanned by its degenerate multiplet partners.**\n\n**But not for every state.** The singlet `{1,1,1,1}` has no partners, yet its `M'(0)` (8 rows) has a 2-dimensional kernel. So part of a kernel can be an artefact of the row choice. Every row satisfies the cross identity, so the partner directions are annihilated by *any* row functional: that part of the kernel is **forced**. The rest is **accidental** and can be lifted by other rows. Using all 32 rows (every pairing `(i,j)`, both ladders) gives the smallest kernel any choice of 8 rows can reach.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 10. Forced kernel: the 32-row zero-twist matrix (all pairings (i,j), both ladders). Exact; memory capped. ---- *)\nClearAll[rowsAll, forcedTab];\nrowsAll = Flatten[Table[{s, {i, j}}, {i, 4}, {j, 4}, {s, 2}], 2];\nforcedTab = MemoryConstrained[Table[With[{M32 = Together[Mp[1, 1, untQ[1, 1, mu], untQ[1, 1, mu], rowsAll]], M8 = Together[Mp[1, 1, untQ[1, 1, mu], untQ[1, 1, mu], rowsDef]]},\n      {mu, 8 - MatrixRank[M8], 8 - MatrixRank[M32], NullSpace[M32]}], {mu, {{2, 2, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 0}, {1, 1, 1, 1}}}], 2*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"];\nIf[StringQ[forcedTab], forcedTab, Grid[Prepend[forcedTab, {\"mu\", \"dim ker, 8 rows (cell 9)\", \"dim ker, all 32 rows = forced\", \"forced kernel (w-coords)\"}], Frame -> All]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
