  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Repeating Appendix N of arXiv:2603.26617 (untwisting su(2))\n\nIn Appendix N, the row without periodic insertion (`α = 1`) is a contour around every pole, i.e. minus the residue at infinity. Its entries are `e^{2φu}`×rational, so they vanish like `(2φ)^{2L-M-β}/(2L-M-β)!` (N3). The leading term of the determinant is then the least-suppressed entry of that row times the complementary minor, which is the untwisted inner product (N4). For su(4), the paper notes that several entries vanish at the same rate, and the determinant becomes a sum of minors.\n\n**Here.** Rows are either **full-contour** rows built from raw twisted `Q_i`, `Q^j` (the `α = 1` analogue; the product carries `e^{(φ_i-φ_j)u}`) or the two **good** rows (regularised `(2,1)` pairing, per ladder), which tend to the untwisted 2x2 `N'`. Columns are the `w` basis. Hope: in the full-contour rows the high-degree insertions of columns 3-8 are less suppressed than columns 1-2. Then the 6x6 block on the vanishing columns dominates, leaving `N'`.\n\n**Step 1: the power matrix.** The leading power of each entry is `log_{10}(|entry(10^{-3})|/|entry(10^{-4})|)`, for the norm of `A = {2,1,1,0}`. Everything is numeric: numeric twisted solve, Hodge duals from numeric Wronskians, residues at 80 digits.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 11. Numeric twisted state + raw and regularised Q-functions; power matrix of full-contour and good rows. h = 1. ---- *)\nClearAll[twStateN, mkQ, fullRow, goodRow, powTab];\ntwStateN[S_, P_, mu_, eps_, prec_] := Module[{Ms = Mdeg[S, P, mu], x, eqs = {}, unk, sols, t0 = N[UntwSolve0[S, P, mu][\"tc\"] /. prm, prec], best},\n   Do[eqs = Join[eqs, DeleteCases[CoefficientList[Expand[BaxRes[S, P, mu][k][qmonic[k, Ms[[k]]]][x] /. zeps[eps]], x], 0]], {k, 4}];\n   unk = Join[tcvars, Flatten[Table[qc[k, j], {k, 4}, {j, 0, Ms[[k]] - 1}]]];\n   sols = NSolve[Thread[eqs == 0], unk, WorkingPrecision -> prec];\n   best = First[SortBy[sols, Norm[(tcvars /. #) - t0] &]];\n   <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"eps\" -> eps, \"tc\" -> (tcvars /. best), \"q\" -> Table[PadRight[CoefficientList[qmonic[k, Ms[[k]]][x] /. best, x], Ms[[k]] + 1], {k, 4}], \"sub\" -> zeps[eps]|>];\n(* raw Q_l = z_l^y q_l(y); raw uncentred Hodge dual Q^l = (-1)^l zeta_l^(y-1) qd_l(y-1); regularised R_k, R^k by matching the untwisted q's at u = 0..3.\n   \"qN\", \"qdN\" expose the raw coefficient lists (ascending) of the q_l and qd_l. *)\nmkQ[S_, P_, mu_, eps_, prec_] := Module[{st = twStateN[S, P, mu, eps, prec], u0 = UntwSolve0[S, P, mu], zN, qN, zeta, qdN, rem, x, Qr, Qdr, A, B, cdir, cdual},\n   zN = N[Table[z[l] /. st[\"sub\"], {l, 4}], prec]; qN = st[\"q\"]; zeta = Table[Times @@ Delete[zN, l], {l, 4}];\n   {qdN, rem} = Transpose[Table[Module[{II = Complement[Range[4], {l}], Wx, Vv, qr},\n       Wx = Expand[Det[Table[zN[[II[[a]]]]^(3 - b) qpoly[qN[[II[[a]]]], x - (b - 1)], {a, 3}, {b, 3}]]];\n       Vv = Product[zN[[II[[a]]]] - zN[[II[[b]]]], {a, 3}, {b, a + 1, 3}];\n       qr = PolynomialQuotientRemainder[Expand[(Wx /. x -> x + 1)/Vv], Expand[AA[S, P][x + 1] /. prm], x];\n       {CoefficientList[qr[[1]], x], Max[Abs[Append[CoefficientList[qr[[2]], x], 0]]]}], {l, 4}]];\n   Qr[l_, y_] := zN[[l]]^y qpoly[qN[[l]], y];\n   Qdr[l_, y_] := (-1)^l zeta[[l]]^(y - 1) qpoly[qdN[[l]], y - 1];\n   A = Table[Qr[l, m], {m, 0, 3}, {l, 4}]; B = Table[Qdr[l, m], {m, 0, 3}, {l, 4}];\n   cdir = Table[LinearSolve[A, Table[qpoly[u0[\"q\"][[k]], m], {m, 0, 3}]], {k, 4}];\n   cdual = Table[LinearSolve[B, Table[qpoly[u0[\"qd\"][k], m], {m, 0, 3}]], {k, 4}];\n   <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"eps\" -> eps, \"tc\" -> st[\"tc\"], \"sub\" -> st[\"sub\"], \"dualRemainder\" -> Max[rem], \"qN\" -> qN, \"qdN\" -> qdN,\n     \"rawdir\" -> Function[{k, y}, Qr[k, y]], \"rawdual\" -> Function[{k, y}, Qdr[k, y]],\n     \"dir\" -> Function[{k, y}, cdir[[k]] . Table[Qr[l, y], {l, 4}]], \"dual\" -> Function[{k, y}, cdual[[k]] . Table[Qdr[l, y], {l, 4}]]|>];\n(* full-contour row (both ladders, raw Q's) and good row (one ladder, regularised Q's): 8-vectors over the w-columns *)\nfullRow[S_, P_, QA_, QB_, {i_, j_}] := Sum[p[[2]] fcol[S, P][Function[y, QA[\"rawdual\"][j, y]], Function[y, QB[\"rawdir\"][i, y]], p[[1]]], {s, 2}, {p, ladder[S, P][s]}];\ngoodRow[S_, P_, QA_, QB_, s_, {i_, j_}] := Sum[p[[2]] fcol[S, P][Function[y, QA[\"dual\"][j, y]], Function[y, QB[\"dir\"][i, y]], p[[1]]], {p, ladder[S, P][s]}];\n(* leading power of each entry from two eps values *)\npowTab[S_, P_, mu_, prec_] := Module[{Q1 = mkQ[S, P, mu, 1/1000, prec], Q2 = mkQ[S, P, mu, 1/10000, prec], rowsF, pw},\n   rowsF = Tuples[Range[4], 2];\n   pw[a_, b_] := MapThread[If[Abs[#1] < 10^-(prec/2) && Abs[#2] < 10^-(prec/2), \"zero\", Round[Log10[Abs[#1]/Abs[#2]], 0.01]] &, {a, b}];\n   <|\"dualRemainder\" -> N[Max[Q1[\"dualRemainder\"], Q2[\"dualRemainder\"]], 3],\n     \"full\" -> Table[Prepend[pw[fullRow[S, P, Q1, Q1, ij], fullRow[S, P, Q2, Q2, ij]], ij], {ij, rowsF}],\n     \"good\" -> Table[Prepend[pw[goodRow[S, P, Q1, Q1, s, {2, 1}], goodRow[S, P, Q2, Q2, s, {2, 1}]], {\"good (2,1)\", s}], {s, 2}]|>];\npowA = MemoryConstrained[TimeConstrained[powTab[1, 1, {2, 1, 1, 0}, 80], 600, \"TIME LIMIT HIT\"], 3*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"];\nIf[StringQ[powA], powA, Column[{Row[{\"max remainder in the Hodge-dual division (must be ~0): \", powA[\"dualRemainder\"]}],\n   Grid[Prepend[Join[powA[\"full\"], powA[\"good\"]], {\"row (i,j)\", \"w1: ∇-col\", \"w2: u^0\", \"w3: u^2\", \"w4: u\", \"w5: ν4\", \"w6: u ν1\", \"w7: u^3\", \"w8: u ν4\"}], Frame -> All]}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"331408\" data-output-id=\"16\" data-out-n=\"118\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"16\" data-sub-start=\"36\" data-sub-end=\"37\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[118]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"7\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:24.04em;vertical-align:-11.77em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.27em;\"><span style=\"top:-25.12em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.69em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">max remainder in the Hodge-dual division (must be ~</span><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0): </span></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.07em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.69em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:11.69em;\"><span style=\"top:-13.65em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:13.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:22.8em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-11.15em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:11.65em;\"><span style=\"top:-13.81em;