   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Results (2026-09-11, (S,P) = (1,1), numeric, 80 digits)\n\n**The twisted norm factorises at leading order in the twist:**\n\n$$\\det M'(\\varepsilon) = \\det[\\text{6 full-contour rows} \\times \\text{cols } 3..8]\\cdot \\det[\\text{2 good rows} \\times \\text{cols } 1,2]\\,\\big(1 + O(\\varepsilon)\\big),\\qquad \\det[\\text{good} \\times \\text{cols } 1,2] \\to N'_{untw} .$$\n\nThe good rows are the regularised `(2,1)` pairing on ladders 1 and 2. Six full-contour rows (raw twisted Q's, no periodic insertion) take columns 3-8.\n\n| state | untwisted N' | 2x2 at ε = 10⁻³, 10⁻⁴ | ratio at ε = 10⁻³, 10⁻⁴ | order of det M' |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `{2,2,0,0}` | −1306.326 | −1292.26, −1304.92 | 1.00130, 1.000130 | 0 |\n| `{2,1,1,0}` | 6661.97 | 6619.98, 6657.68 | 1.00286, 1.000286 | 2 |\n| `{1,1,1,1}` | −427/3 | −142.33302, −142.3333302 | 1.00602, 1.000601 | 8 |\n\nThose rows are `(2,1), (3,1), (4,1), (3,2), (4,2), (4,3)`. For `{2,1,1,0}` two other choices of the six full rows, mixing in the diagonal rows `(1,1), (2,2), (3,3)` or `(1,1), (2,2), (4,4)`, give the same limit (ratios 1.00209 → 1.000208 and 1.00122 → 1.000122).\n\n**Why (power matrix, cell 17).** In every full-contour row the powers follow the same offset profile across the columns, `(0, 0, -2, -1, -2, -3, -3, -3)`, so columns 1-2 are the most suppressed. The minimal-power Laplace term therefore pairs the full rows with columns 3-8 and the good rows with columns 1-2. This is the su(4) version of Appendix N's (N3)-(N4), with the IoM reduction removing the \"several entries vanish at the same rate\" problem between columns 1-2 and 3-8.\n\n**Observations, not derived.** The order of `det M'` with these raw rows is `8 - Σ_{i<j}(μ_i - μ_j)` for all three states. It reflects the normalisation of the raw Q-functions, like the `φ^{L-M_A-M_B}` prefactor in (N4). The closed form of the leading coefficient of the 6x6 block is still open; in Appendix N it is `(2φ)^k/k!`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Does the 6x6 block simplify?\n\n**Measurement.** For each state and several twist **rays** `z_j = 1 + ε a_j` (`j = 1,2,3`), `z_4 = 1/∏`, so that `φ ≈ ε (a_1, a_2, a_3, -a_1-a_2-a_3)`, compute the 6x6 block `m_6(ε)` (rows `(2,1),(3,1),(4,1),(3,2),(4,2),(4,3)`, columns 3-8). Read its power `p` and the leading coefficient `C_6 = lim m_6/ε^p` (Richardson from `ε = 10^{-4}, 10^{-5}`).\n\n- **Pure twist factor:** `C_6(ray)` should be a product of powers of `(a_i - a_j)`, and depend only mildly on the state.\n- **Untwisted Q's at the inhomogeneities:** at a fixed ray, the ratios between states should match ratios of untwisted Q-values.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 14. m6 = det[full rows (set 1) x cols 3..8]: power and leading coefficient, per state and twist ray. ---- *)\nClearAll[m6Of, rayData, rays];\nm6Of[S_, P_, mu_, fullSet_, eps_, prec_] := Module[{Q = mkQ[S, P, mu, eps, prec]}, Det[Table[fullRow[S, P, Q, Q, ij][[3 ;; 8]], {ij, fullSet}]]];\n(* Block temporarily replaces the twist ray used by every solver *)\nrayData[S_, P_, mu_, ray_, prec_] := Block[{zeps},\n   zeps[e_] := Join[prm, {z[1] -> 1 + e ray[[1]], z[2] -> 1 + e ray[[2]], z[3] -> 1 + e ray[[3]], z[4] -> 1/((1 + e ray[[1]]) (1 + e ray[[2]]) (1 + e ray[[3]]))}];\n   Module[{es = {1/1000, 1/10000, 1/100000}, m, p, c},\n    m = Table[m6Of[S, P, mu, blockSets[[1]], e, prec], {e, es}];\n    p = Round[Log10[Abs[m[[1]]/m[[2]]]]]; c = m/es^p;\n    {mu, ray, p, N[c, 8], N[(10 c[[3]] - c[[2]])/9, 12]}]];\nrays = {{1, 1/3, -1/2}, {2, -1, 1/2}, {1, 3, -2}, {-1, 2, 1/4}};\nC6Tab = MemoryConstrained[TimeConstrained[Flatten[Table[rayData[1, 1, mu, r, 100], {mu, {{2, 2, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 0}, {1, 1, 1, 1}}}, {r, rays}], 1], 1400, \"TIME LIMIT HIT\"], 3*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"];\nIf[StringQ[C6Tab], C6Tab, Grid[Prepend[C6Tab, {\"mu\", \"ray a\", \"power p\", \"m6/eps^p at eps = 1e-3, 1e-4, 1e-5\", \"C6 (Richardson)\"}], Frame -> All]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
