   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Pure-twist-factor test.** Ray `(1, 3, -2)` above is degenerate (`a_4 = a_3 = -2`, so `z_3` and `z_4` collide at first order) and is discarded. For ten generic rays, fit\n\n$$\\log|C_6| = \\log|K| + \\sum_{i<j} n_{ij}\\,\\log|a_i - a_j| ,\\qquad a_4 = -(a_1+a_2+a_3) .$$\n\nIf `C_6` is a pure twist factor, the six exponents `n_{ij}` come out integers with small residuals, and `K = C_6/\\prod a_{ij}^{n_{ij}}` is the same on every ray.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Results: the leading coefficient of the 6x6 block (cell 24; ten generic rays, `φ ≈ ε a`)\n\n| state | power p | fitted exponents on `(a_12, a_13, a_14, a_23, a_24, a_34)` | max log residual |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `{1,1,1,1}` | 8 | 2.0000000, 1.0000000, 0.0000000, 2.0000004, 0.9999999, 1.9999999 | ~10⁻⁷ |\n| `{2,1,1,0}` | 2 | 2.27, 2.80, −8.45, −7.55, 1.80, 6.65 | 3.9 |\n| `{2,2,0,0}` | 0 | 4.21, −2.33, −4.90, 1.92, −0.47, 1.68 | 1.7 |\n\nThe power `p` is the same on all ten rays for each state, so the rays are generic.\n\n**Singlet: a pure twist factor.** `K = C_6/(a_12^2 a_13 a_23^2 a_24 a_34^2) = -1/2` on all ten rays (spread `9×10^{-7}`, the Richardson accuracy):\n\n$$m_6 = -\\tfrac12\\,(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)^2(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_3)(\\varphi_2-\\varphi_3)^2(\\varphi_2-\\varphi_4)(\\varphi_3-\\varphi_4)^2\\,\\big(1+O(\\varepsilon)\\big) .$$\n\nSo for `{1,1,1,1}` the twisted norm untwists to this twist factor times the 2x2 `N' = -427/3`, at leading order.\n\n**Non-singlets: not a single monomial in the raw normalisation.** Likely cause: the singlet has equal degrees `M = (1,1,1,1)`, so its raw monic `q_k` stay finite. For `{2,1,1,0}` and `{2,2,0,0}` some raw `q_k` diverge like `ε^{-(M_k-M_1)}`, with coefficients that are sums of rational functions of the `a_i`, which would turn a product into a sum. To be tested with a normalisation of the full-row Q-functions that removes the divergence.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Option 1: normalise away the divergence of the raw Q's.** Each raw polynomial (direct `q_k`, dual `q^j`) is divided by its most divergent coefficient. The rule: measure each coefficient's growth from `ε = 10^{-4}` to `10^{-5}`, take the highest-degree coefficient among those with maximal growth. Rescaling the Q's divides each full row `(i,j)` by `n^{dual}_j n^{dir}_i`, so\n\n$$m_6^{norm} = m_6^{raw} \\Big/ \\prod_{\\text{rows }(i,j)} n^{dual}_j\\, n^{dir}_i .$$\n\nThe same fit as above is then applied to `C_6^{norm}`. Control: the singlet's polynomials do not diverge, so the rule picks the monic leading coefficient and its result `-1/2 \\cdot a_{12}^2 a_{13} a_{23}^2 a_{24} a_{34}^2` must be unchanged. The chosen coefficient `u^j` for each polynomial is reported per ray; it must not change from ray to ray.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 16. Normalised 6x6 block: divide each raw Q by its most divergent coefficient; leading coefficient and fit per state. ---- *)\nClearAll[pickNorm, C6norm];\n(* index (1-based) of the highest-degree coefficient among those growing fastest between the two eps *)\npickNorm[c1_List, c2_List] := Module[{d = Table[If[Abs[c1[[j]]] < 10^-40 || Abs[c2[[j]]] < 10^-40, -Infinity, Log10[Abs[c2[[j]]/c1[[j]]]]], {j, Length[c1]}], dm}, dm = Max[d]; Max[Flatten[Position[d, x_ /; x > dm - 1/2]]]];\nC6norm[S_, P_, mu_, ray_, prec_] := Block[{zeps},\n   zeps[e_] := Join[prm, {z[1] -> 1 + e ray[[1]], z[2] -> 1 + e ray[[2]], z[3] -> 1 + e ray[[3]], z[4] -> 1/((1 + e ray[[1]]) (1 + e ray[[2]]) (1 + e ray[[3]]))}];\n   Module[{es = {1/10000, 1/100000}, Qs, m, jq, jd, nrm, mn, p, c},\n    Qs = Table[mkQ[S, P, mu, e, prec], {e, es}];\n    m = Table[Det[Table[fullRow[S, P, Q, Q, ij][[3 ;; 8]], {ij, blockSets[[1]]}]], {Q, Qs}];\n    jq = Table[pickNorm[Qs[[1]][\"qN\"][[k]], Qs[[2]][\"qN\"][[k]]], {k, 4}];\n    jd = Table[pickNorm[Qs[[1]][\"qdN\"][[k]], Qs[[2]][\"qdN\"][[k]]], {k, 4}];\n    nrm = Table[Times @@ Table[Q[\"qdN\"][[ij[[2]]]][[jd[[ij[[2]]]]]] Q[\"qN\"][[ij[[1]]]][[jq[[ij[[1]]]]]], {ij, blockSets[[1]]}], {Q, Qs}];\n    mn = m/nrm; p = Round[Log10[Abs[mn[[1]]/mn[[2]]]]]; c = mn/es^p;\n    {ray, p, (10 c[[2]] - c[[1]])/9, jq - 1, jd - 1}]];\nC6normData = MemoryConstrained[TimeConstrained[Table[{mu, Table[C6norm[1, 1, mu, r, 100], {r, raysG}]}, {mu, {{2, 1, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0, 0}, {1, 1, 1, 1}}}], 1700, \"TIME LIMIT HIT\"], 3*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"];\nC6normFits = If[StringQ[C6normData], C6normData, Table[Join[<|\"mu\" -> d[[1]], \"p per ray\" -> d[[2, All, 2]], \"direct u^j per ray\" -> Union[d[[2, All, 4]]], \"dual u^j per ray\" -> Union[d[[2, All, 5]]]|>, fitC6[{#[[1]], #[[2]], #[[3]]} & /@ d[[2]]]], {d, C6normData}]];\nIf[StringQ[C6normFits], C6normFits, Grid[Prepend[Values /@ C6normFits, Keys[First[C6normFits]]], Frame -> All]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
