   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Which six full-contour rows give a pure twist factor?\n\nThe 6x6 block is not unique. For each state and each of the ten rays, all 16 full-contour rows (every pairing `(i,j)`, raw Q's) are computed once on columns 3-8 at `ε = 10^{-4}, 10^{-5}`. Then **all C(16,6) = 8008** row choices are scanned. For each choice: the power must be the same on every ray, the leading coefficient comes from Richardson extrapolation, and it is fitted to `K ∏ a_{ij}^{n_{ij}}`. A choice gives a pure twist factor when the fit residual is small, the exponents are integers, and `K` is the same on every ray.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 18. Row data (16 full rows x cols 3..8) per state, ray, eps; then scan all 6-row subsets for product form.\n   Zero test is PRECISION-aware: a determinant is skipped only if exactly zero or with < 10 significant digits left\n   (an absolute threshold wrongly discarded genuine small values such as the singlet's eps^8 block). ---- *)\nClearAll[rowData, subsetScan, pairs16];\npairs16 = Tuples[Range[4], 2];\nrowData[S_, P_, mu_, ray_, prec_] := Block[{zeps},\n   zeps[e_] := Join[prm, {z[1] -> 1 + e ray[[1]], z[2] -> 1 + e ray[[2]], z[3] -> 1 + e ray[[3]], z[4] -> 1/((1 + e ray[[1]]) (1 + e ray[[2]]) (1 + e ray[[3]]))}];\n   Table[With[{Q = mkQ[S, P, mu, e, prec]}, N[Table[fullRow[S, P, Q, Q, ij][[3 ;; 8]], {ij, pairs16}], 60]], {e, {1/10000, 1/100000}}]];\nRD = MemoryConstrained[TimeConstrained[Table[{mu, Table[rowData[1, 1, mu, r, 100], {r, raysG}]}, {mu, {{2, 2, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 0}, {1, 1, 1, 1}}}], 1200, \"TIME LIMIT HIT\"], 3*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"];\nsubsetScan[s_] := Module[{data = RD[[s, 2]], X = N[Table[Prepend[Log[Abs[aDiffs[r]]], 1], {r, raysG}], 30], res = {}},\n   Do[Module[{m = Table[Det[data[[r, e]][[sub]]], {r, 10}, {e, 2}], p, C, sol, resid, nR, K},\n      If[AnyTrue[Flatten[m], # == 0 || Precision[#] < 10 &], Continue[]];\n      p = Round[Log10[Abs[m[[All, 1]]/m[[All, 2]]]]]; If[Length[Union[p]] > 1, Continue[]];\n      C = Table[(10 m[[r, 2]]/(1/100000)^p[[r]] - m[[r, 1]]/(1/10000)^p[[r]])/9, {r, 10}];\n      sol = LeastSquares[X, Log[Abs[C]]]; resid = Max[Abs[X . sol - Log[Abs[C]]]];\n      nR = Round[Rest[sol]]; K = Table[C[[r]]/Times @@ (aDiffs[raysG[[r]]]^nR), {r, 10}];\n      AppendTo[res, {pairs16[[sub]], p[[1]], N[resid, 3], nR, N[Mean[K], 10], N[(Max[K] - Min[K])/Abs[Mean[K]], 3]}]], {sub, Subsets[Range[16], {6}]}];\n   res];\nscanRes = If[StringQ[RD], RD, MemoryConstrained[TimeConstrained[Table[{RD[[s, 1]], subsetScan[s]}, {s, 3}], 1500, \"TIME LIMIT HIT\"], 3*10^9, \"MEMORY LIMIT HIT\"]];\nscanSummary = If[StringQ[scanRes], scanRes, Table[With[{all = sr[[2]], good = Select[sr[[2]], #[[3]] < 10^-4 && #[[6]] < 10^-4 &]}, {sr[[1]], Length[all], Length[good], Tally[good[[All, 2]]], Take[SortBy[good, #[[2]] &], UpTo[4]]}], {sr, scanRes}]];\nIf[StringQ[scanSummary], scanSummary, Grid[Prepend[scanSummary, {\"mu\", \"#subsets with consistent power\", \"#subsets giving a pure twist product\", \"their powers (tally)\", \"examples {rows, p, resid, exponents, K, spread}\"}], Frame -> All]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
