  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Scan result (cell 31, after fixing the zero test).** Pure twist products exist for every state: `{2,2,0,0}` 321, `{2,1,1,0}` 282, `{1,1,1,1}` 5176 of the 8008 row choices. The powers are 12-17, 8-15 and 8-9 respectively. The non-product behaviour of row set 1 was specific to that choice. To compare the constants `K(μ)` across states (Paul's `Q_12(θ)` hint), the **same** row choice must be a pure product for all three states. The cell below finds those choices.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 18b. Row choices that are pure twist products for ALL three states; powers, exponents and K per state. ---- *)\nClearAll[goodOf, commonSets, commonTab];\ngoodOf[s_] := Association[(#[[1]] -> #) & /@ Select[scanRes[[s, 2]], #[[3]] < 10^-4 && #[[6]] < 10^-4 &]];\ncommonSets = Intersection @@ (Keys[goodOf[#]] & /@ {1, 2, 3});\ncommonTab = Table[With[{g = goodOf /@ {1, 2, 3}}, {cs, g[[1, Key[cs], 2]], g[[2, Key[cs], 2]], g[[3, Key[cs], 2]], g[[1, Key[cs], 4]], g[[2, Key[cs], 4]], g[[3, Key[cs], 4]], g[[1, Key[cs], 5]], g[[2, Key[cs], 5]], g[[3, Key[cs], 5]]}], {cs, commonSets}];\nColumn[{Row[{\"row choices that are pure products for all three states: \", Length[commonSets]}],\n  Grid[Prepend[Take[commonTab, UpTo[12]], {\"six rows (i,j)\", \"p {2,2,0,0}\", \"p {2,1,1,0}\", \"p {1,1,1,1}\", \"exps {2,2,0,0}\", \"exps {2,1,1,0}\", \"exps {1,1,1,1}\", \"K {2,2,0,0}\", \"K {2,1,1,0}\", \"K {1,1,1,1}\"}], Frame -> All]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
